          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 82582,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wir werden oft auf verschiedene Datensätze stoßen, die wir zu einem kombinieren sollten, wie zum Beispiel den Wert der Verkäufe über das Wochenende.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"sales_sat = [\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"22\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"sales_sun = [\" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Plus operator",
            "id": 82583,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um zwei Datensätze zu kombinieren, wie die in <code>dataset_1</code> und <code>dataset_2</code>, verwenden wir die Namen der Listen und den <code>+</code>-Operator.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(dataset_1 + dataset_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"69\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>dataset_1</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>dataset_2</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Verbinde zwei Listen mit <code>+</code>. Die Werte der linken Liste stehen vor den Werten der rechten Liste.</p><p>Verbinde die Datensätze, sodass der Code <code>[4, 5, 1, 2, 3]</code> ausgibt.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"[\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"[\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\",\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"dataset_2\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"+\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"dataset_1\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"57\" /><option startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[4, 5, 1, 2, 3]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>dataset_2</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>dataset_1</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Appended at the end",
            "id": 82584,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wenn du <code>+</code> verwendest, wird die zweite Liste am Ende der ersten Liste angehängt.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(dataset_1 + dataset_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"58\" endIndex=\"59\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>+</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Different types",
            "id": 82585,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wir können <code>+</code> auch verwenden, um Listen mit verschiedenen Arten von Werten zu kombinieren, wie die numerischen <code>seats</code> und die booleschen <code>taken</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"seats = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"taken = [\" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(seats + taken)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"5\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"23\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>seats</code>, gefolgt von <code>taken</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Mit <code>+</code> kannst du Listen verbinden, die verschiedene Wertetypen enthalten.</p><p>Verbinde die Zahlen in <code>seats</code> und die Booleans in <code>taken</code>, mit den Sitzen zuerst, sodass der Code <code>[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]</code> ausgibt.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"seats = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"taken = [\" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"True\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"False\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(seats + taken)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"58\" /><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"60\" /><option startIndex=\"61\" endIndex=\"66\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, True, True, False]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>seats</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>taken</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Save in variable",
            "id": 82586,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Um die kombinierte Liste wiederzuverwenden, können wir sie in einer Variable speichern, wie hier mit <code>combined</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"combined = dataset_1 + dataset_2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(combined)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"74\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>combined</code>, gefolgt von <code>=</code> und schließlich <code>dataset_1 + dataset_2</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Füge die beiden Datensätze zusammen, zuerst <code>dataset_1</code>, und speichere das Ergebnis in <code>combined</code>, damit der Code <code>[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]</code> ausgibt.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"dataset_1 = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"dataset_2 = [\" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"combined = dataset_1 + dataset_2\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(combined)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"50\" /><option startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"52\" /><option startIndex=\"53\" endIndex=\"62\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>combined</code>, gefolgt von <code>=</code>, <code>dataset_1</code>, <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>dataset_2</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Plus operator",
            "id": 82669,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was macht der <code>+</code> Operator, wenn er auf zwei Listen angewendet wird?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Es verbindet die Elemente der beiden Listen zu einer neuen Liste</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Es fügt jedes Element aus einer Liste zu jedem Element der anderen hinzu</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Es verbindet die Elemente der beiden Listen zu einer neuen Liste.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Welche neue Liste erstellt <code>[1, 2] + [3, 4]</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[1, 2, 3, 4]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>[4, 6]</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[[1, 2], [3, 4]]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>[1, 2, 3, 4]</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Appended at the end",
            "id": 82670,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wenn du <code>list_1 + list_2</code> codierst, in welcher Reihenfolge erscheinen die Elemente in der neuen Liste?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Die Elemente von <code>list_1</code> erscheinen zuerst, dann die von <code>list_2</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Die Elemente beider Listen werden zufällig gemischt</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Die Elemente von <code>list_1</code> erscheinen zuerst, dann die von <code>list_2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wenn <code>first = [\"A\", \"B\"]</code> und <code>second = [\"C\", \"D\"]</code> gilt, was erstellt <code>first + second</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"C\", \"D\", \"A\", \"B\"]</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"A\", \"C\", \"B\", \"D\"]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\"]</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Different types",
            "id": 82671,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Welche Arten von Werten können die Listen haben, die wir kombinieren?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Jeder Typ</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Nur derselbe Typ</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Jeder Typ.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Was erstellt <code>[\"id\"] + [7, True]</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>[\"id\", 7, True]</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Es verursacht einen Fehler, weil die Werttypen unterschiedlich sind.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>[\"id\", \"7\", \"True\"]</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>[\"id\", 7, True]</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Save in variable",
            "id": 82672,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Wie können wir die Liste, die wir durch das Zusammenfügen von zwei Listen erhalten, wiederverwenden?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Wir speichern es in einer Variable</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Wir können es nicht wiederverwenden, wir können es nur einmal anzeigen</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wir speichern es in einer Variable.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Du musst das Ergebnis von <code>first + second</code> später wiederverwenden. Welche Zeile speichert diese zusammengefügte Liste?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>combined = first + second</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>print(first + second)</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>first + second</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>combined = first + second</code> aus.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Plus operator ",
            "id": 82674,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code <code>+</code>, um die beiden Listen zu verbinden, die die Wachstumsrate einer Pflanze speichern.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"growth_rate_1 = [\" /><text value=\"0.5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.7\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"growth_rate_2 = [\" /><text value=\"0.8\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(growth_rate_1 + growth_rate_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"86\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"[0.5, 0.7, 0.8, 0.8, 0.6, 0.6]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Gib <code>+</code> ein.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Appended at the end",
            "id": 82676,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Verbinde die <code>customers</code> und <code>order_number</code> Listen, sodass die Namen der Kunden zuerst kommen.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"customers = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Jess&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mike&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lynn&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"order_number = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(customers + order_number)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"93\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>customers</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>order_number</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Füge <code>customers</code> und <code>order_number</code> zusammen, sodass die Namen zuerst kommen und <code>['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]</code> ausgegeben wird.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"customers = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Jess&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mike&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Lynn&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"order_number = [\" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(customers + order_number)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Jess', 'Mike', 'Lynn', 3, 1, 2]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>customers</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>order_number</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Different types",
            "id": 82675,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Verbinde die Listen <code>t⁠e⁠a⁠m⁠_⁠1</code> und <code>t⁠e⁠a⁠m⁠_⁠2</code>, sodass die Spielernamen und Punktzahlen in einer einzigen Liste ausgegeben werden.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"team_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ana&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"78\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"57\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sam&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(team_1 + team_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"86\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>+</code>, gefolgt von <code>team_2</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Füge <code>team_1</code> und <code>team_2</code> zu einer Liste zusammen, zuerst <code>team_1</code>, damit der Code <code>['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]</code> ausgibt.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"team_1 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Ana&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"78\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joe&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"team_2 = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Kim&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"57\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Sam&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(team_1 + team_2)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"77\" /><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"['Ana', 78, 'Joe', 80, 'Kim', 57, 'Sam', 60]\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Wähle <code>team_1</code>, gefolgt von <code>+</code> und schließlich <code>team_2</code> aus.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Save in variable",
            "id": 82677,
            "contentType": "interactive",
